(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_botany_celltheunitoflife=[{id:"neet-2026-q092",pn:92,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Nucleus and nucleolus",q:"Which one of the following is the site for active ribosomal RNA synthesis?",o:["Nucleolus","Chromatin","Centrosome","Kinetochore"],c:0,s:"The nucleolus is the site of active ribosomal RNA synthesis."},{id:"neet-2026r-q097",pn:97,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Cell organelles structure",q:`Match List-I with List-II.
A. Cristae \u2014 I. Flat membrane sacs in stroma of chloroplast
B. Cisternae \u2014 II. Infoldings in mitochondria
C. Thylakoids \u2014 III. Cell membrane
D. Phospholipid \u2014 IV. Disc shaped sacs in the Golgi apparatus
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III","A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I","A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II","A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II"],c:0,s:`Cristae \u2192 Infoldings in mitochondria.
Cisternae \u2192 Disc shaped sacs in the Golgi apparatus.
Thylakoids \u2192 Flat membrane sacs in stroma of chloroplast.
Phospholipid \u2192 Cell membrane.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q103",pn:103,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Endoplasmic reticulum",q:"Smooth endoplasmic reticulum ___________ .",o:["is the major site for the synthesis of lipids","is actively involved in protein synthesis","is a site for the synthesis of carbohydrates","has ribosomes attached to its surface"],c:0,s:`Smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER) makes lipids and steroidal hormones.
It has no ribosomes on it, so it looks smooth.
Rough ER is the one actively involved in protein synthesis.
Carbohydrate synthesis occurs in chloroplasts.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q108",pn:108,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Cell theory",q:"Cell theory was formulated by ______________.",o:["Robert Brown","Singer and Nicolson","Antonie Von Leeuwenhoek","Schleiden and Schwann"],c:3,s:"Cell theory was formulated by Schleiden and Schwann."},{id:"neet-2026r-q111",pn:111,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Prokaryotic cell",q:`Which of the following are characteristics of prokaryotic cells?
(a) Ribosomes are made of 50S and 30S subunits
(b) They can have plasmids
(c) They contain mesosome
(d) They have peroxisomes
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["(a) and (c) only","(a), (c) and (d) only","(a), (b) and (c) only","(b) and (c) only"],c:2,s:`Ribosomes are made of 50S and 30S subunits (70S ribosomes).
They can have plasmids (extra-chromosomal DNA).
They contain mesosomes (infoldings of the plasma membrane).
They do not have membrane-bound organelles such as peroxisomes.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q113",pn:113,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Endomembrane system",q:"Endomembrane system includes _______.",o:["endoplasmic reticulum, chloroplast, peroxisomes and vacuole","mitochondria, chloroplast, peroxisomes and vacuole","Golgi complex, chloroplast, peroxisomes and vacuole","endoplasmic reticulum, Golgi complex, lysosomes and vacuole"],c:3,s:`The endomembrane system includes organelles whose functions are coordinated.
It has four organelles: endoplasmic reticulum, Golgi body, lysosomes and vacuole.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q116",pn:116,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Plastids",q:"The plastid that stores xanthophyll is known as ___________.",o:["chromoplast","aleuroplast","amyloplast","chloroplast"],c:0,s:"The plastid that stores xanthophyll is called a chromoplast."},{id:"neet-2026r-q121",pn:121,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Mitochondria",q:"Mitochondrial inner membrane encloses ___________ .",o:["cytosol","mucus","aqueous humor","matrix"],c:3,s:"The mitochondrial inner membrane encloses the matrix."},{id:"neet-2026-q148",pn:148,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Cell organelles",q:"Non-membrane bound cell organelles found in both prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells are ____ .",o:["Centrosomes","Ribosomes","Lysosomes","Mitochondria"],c:1,s:"Ribosome is a non-membrane bound cell organelle found in both prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells."},{id:"neet-2026-q152",pn:152,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Cell organelles and inclusions",q:`Choose the correct statements regarding cell organelles and their inclusions.
A. The endomembrane system includes Golgi complex, endoplasmic reticulum and mitochondria.
B. Rough endoplasmic reticulum bears ribosomes on its surface.
C. Both mitochondria and plastids have circular DNA.
D. A network of microtubules, microfilaments and intermediate filaments present in the cytoplasm is called cytoskeleton.
E. Mitochondrion is a single membrane-bound structure.`,o:["C, D and E only","A and B only","A, B and C only","B, C and D only"],c:3,s:`The endomembrane system does not include mitochondria, so A is wrong.
Mitochondria are double membrane bound organelles, so E is wrong.
B, C and D are correct.`},{id:"neet-2026-q163",pn:163,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Cell membrane",q:`Select the correct statements regarding cell membrane in eukaryotic cell.
A. Membrane of human RBCs has approximately 52% protein.
B. Major phospholipids are arranged in a bilayer.
C. Extensions of the plasma membrane into the cell form mesosomes.
D. Tails towards the inner part of lipids are hydrophobic and thus protected from aqueous medium.
E. Glycocalyx is present on the outer surface of the plasma membrane.`,o:["A, C and E only","B, C and E only","C, D and E only","A, B and D only"],c:3,s:`In prokaryotes, extensions of the plasma membrane into the cell form mesosomes. Eukaryotes lack such structures, so C is wrong.
Glycocalyx is present on the outer surface of the plasma membrane in prokaryotes. Eukaryotes do not have glycocalyx, so E is wrong.
Hence only statements A, B and D are correct.`},{id:"neet-2025-q098",pn:98,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Ribosomes",q:`From the statements given below choose the correct option :
A. The eukaryotic ribosomes are 80S and prokaryotic ribosomes are 70S.
B. Each ribosome has two sub-units.
C. The two sub-units of 80S ribosome are 60S and 40S while that of 70S are 50S and 30S.
D. The two sub-units of 80S ribosome are 60S and 20S and that of 70S are 50S and 20S.
E. The two sub-units of 80S are 60S and 30S and that of 70S are 50S and 30S.`,o:["A, B, C are true","A, B, D are true","A, B, E are true","B, D, E are true"],c:0,s:`Eukaryotic ribosomes are 80S and prokaryotic ribosomes are 70S.
Each ribosome has two sub-units.
The sub-units of 80S are 60S and 40S, and those of 70S are 50S and 30S.
So A, B and C are true.`},{id:"neet-2025-q121",pn:121,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Cell structures and functions",q:`Match List-I with List-II.
List-I: A. Centromere; B. Cilium; C. Cristae; D. Cell membrane
List-II: I. Mitochondrion; II. Cell division; III. Cell movement; IV. Phospholipid Bilayer`,o:["A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV","A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III","A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV"],c:3,s:`Centromere helps in cell division.
Cilium helps in cell movement.
Cristae are finger-like structures of mitochondria.
Cell membrane is a phospholipid bilayer.`},{id:"neet-2025-q128",pn:128,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Prokaryotic cell",q:"A specialised membranous structure in a prokaryotic cell which helps in cell well wall formation, DNA replication and respiration is",o:["Mesosome","Chromatophores","Cristae","Endoplasmic Reticulum"],c:0,s:`Mesosome is a membranous extension in the bacterial cell.
It helps in cell wall formation and DNA replication, and has enzymes for respiration.`},{id:"neet-2025-q140",pn:140,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Cell: The Unit of Life",st:"Golgi apparatus",q:`Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion (A), and the other is labelled as Reason (R).
Assertion (A) : The primary function of the Golgi apparatus is to package the materials made by the endoplasmic reticulum and deliver it to intracellular targets and outside the cell.
Reason (R) : Vesicles containing materials made by the endoplasmic reticulum fuse with the cis face of the Golgi apparatus, and they are modified and released from the trans face of the Golgi apparatus.
In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A","Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A","A is true but R is false","A is false but R is true"],c:1,s:`The primary function of the Golgi apparatus is to package materials made by the endoplasmic reticulum and deliver them to intracellular targets and outside the cell, so the assertion is correct.
The reason is also correct.
Golgi apparatus stays in close association with the endoplasmic reticulum.
Both statements are correct but the reason does not explain the assertion.`}]})();
